# Regression: queue row click panics on stale captured index.
#
# Bug history (2026-05-08):
#   crates/app-gpui/components/home/queue.rs used `state.app.queue_state[idx]`
#   inside an `on_mouse_up` listener whose `idx` was captured at render time.
#   When the queue mutated (cleared, items removed) between paint and click,
#   the listener fired with a stale idx and panicked with
#   "the len is 0 but the index is 0", then escalated to abort because the
#   panic crossed an FFI boundary in gpui_macos::window::handle_view_event.
#
# Fix (queue.rs:170): bounds-check via `.get(idx)` in both left- and
# right-click handlers. The defensive code path is also covered by the
# direct unit tests in crates/app-gpui/tests; this scenario provides the
# end-to-end smoke check that the click handler is wired correctly and
# survives a click-then-clear round trip.
#
# Reproducible run (assumes the QA dir is pre-seeded with at least one
# track — bare `mktemp -d` is empty and the click verbs below will bail
# with "selector not registered"; that's expected and is itself a useful
# guard against the row painter regressing):
#
#   QA_DIR=$(mktemp -d)
#   cp some-tracks/*.flac "$QA_DIR/library/"   # if you have a fixture
#   cargo run -p sotf-gpui --features dev-api --bin sotf-desktop -- --qa "$QA_DIR" &
#   cargo run -p sotf-dev-driver -- crates/sotf-dev-driver/scenarios/queue_stale_index.scn -v

focus       library
assert      screen.focused == "Library"
assert      queue.length == 0

# Populate the queue. With an empty QA library FillQueueMagic adds zero
# tracks and the rest of the scenario short-circuits at the first click.
action      FillQueueMagic
sleep       1s

# Tracked-selector listing — useful when the queue stayed empty so it's
# obvious from the log that `queue.row.0` simply isn't registered.
elements

# Phase 1: click on a live row. Hits the on_mouse_up closure with a
# valid idx; succeeds whether or not the .get(idx) guard exists.
click       queue.row.0
sleep       100ms
assert      queue.current_index == 0

# Phase 2: clear the queue. The row's painted bounds and listener will
# disappear on the next repaint. The deterministic part of the
# regression check is below: query state after a click+clear round
# trip to prove the dev-API server (and the GPUI main thread it
# depends on) didn't go down.
action      ClearQueue
sleep       200ms
assert      queue.length == 0
assert      screen.focused == "Library"

# Phase 3: re-fill and re-click to confirm the click path stays
# healthy after a clear cycle. The pre-fix code would happily survive
# this too — the bug only manifested when the click fired against a
# stale captured idx, which requires racing the paint cycle. The
# narrow race isn't reliably reproducible from a remote HTTP driver
# (paint usually wins by the time the click POST lands), so we test
# what we can: the click path on a populated queue.
action      FillQueueMagic
sleep       500ms
click       queue.row.0
sleep       100ms
assert      queue.current_index == 0
